{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1290,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you know the explanation for why the sky's\nblue, you've heard that sunlight is white"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5350,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light composed of many frequencies and that\nhigher frequency, bluer, light scatters in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9190,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the air more than lower frequency, redder,\nlight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11510,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, you might ask \"why isn't the sky violet,\nsince violet is an even higher frequency than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15920,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "blue?\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16920,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First off, ultraviolet light and x-rays are\nalso higher frequency than blue, and that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20560,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't mean the sky is the color of x-rays…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22820,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Both because we can't see them and also because\nthe sun doesn't make very many of them and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26700,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the atmosphere blocks them all - which\nis probably why we didn't evolve to be able"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30290,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to see them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31290,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And secondly, the color violet in the rainbow\nis the \"roses are red, violets are BLUE\" violet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36750,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not purple – it's dark blue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38890,
    "dDurationMs": 2930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To see why, check out this Chromaticity Diagram!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41820,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a graph of all possible colors as perceived\nby non-colorblind humans, ignoring brightness"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46450,
    "dDurationMs": 1330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and context."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47780,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The color displayed on the diagram is just\nto give you a rough idea – unfortunately"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51810,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your computer can't display all possible perceived\ncolors – it can just display the ones inside"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56470,
    "dDurationMs": 3350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a triangle like this, and is pretending for\nthe rest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59820,
    "dDurationMs": 4079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Single frequency light like that from a laser\nor from splitting white light into a rainbow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63899,
    "dDurationMs": 4561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is graphed around this outside edge, while\nany color anywhere on the inside or along"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68460,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the bottom edge can only be made with a combination\nof various frequencies of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72860,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you can see, pink, purple and magenta can\nonly be made using multiple frequencies of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77030,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light - there is no single frequency of light\nthat's pink - and of course, white light is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81100,
    "dDurationMs": 1150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a mixture as well!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82250,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is why you don't see any of these colors\nin rainbows made from prisms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85850,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But back to the Chromaticity diagram!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87740,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See this line in the middle?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89330,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This shows what color hot objects glow - we\nhave red hot, then white hot, then blue hot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94630,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of these \"hot\" colors are made up of a\nbroad range of frequencies, since that's what"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98330,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hot objects emit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99330,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The sun, for example, is white hot before\nit hits the atmosphere, then its light is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103840,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "split by scattering off of air molecules so\nthe sun looks slightly red hot and the rest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107890,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the sky looks kind of blue hot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109930,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like this picture of a sunset!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111460,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the thing is this - if you notice the\nline for hot-object color, well, it stops"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115910,
    "dDurationMs": 2709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the middle of the diagram near whitish-blue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118619,
    "dDurationMs": 1691,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It never goes beyond that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120310,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's because the spectrum of light from\nan object hotter than the sun always has a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123900,
    "dDurationMs": 4669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "decreasing tail, with slightly more blue than\ngreen than red, so you never get the right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128569,
    "dDurationMs": 4221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "combination of frequencies to push the color\ntowards purple, or for that matter, even towards"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132790,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a pure, deep violet blue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134930,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kind of like how you can mix flour and water\nin different ratios to make bread, pancakes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139090,
    "dDurationMs": 4739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or vegetarian gravy, but as long as you have\nflour in there, your gravy won't be gluten"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143829,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "free."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144829,
    "dDurationMs": 2501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's why the sky appears blueish white."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147330,
    "dDurationMs": 40749,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's basically gravy."
    } ]
  } ]
}
